            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0048" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg40"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10300a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-28T14:00:00-05:00">September 28, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Please immediately communicate to the Secretary General of the League of
                    Nations and suggest to him that he may care to inform the Assembly at its
                    meeting today of the text of a statement which I am making public today reading
                    as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Department of State has been informed by the American Minister to
                            Switzerland of the text of the resolution unanimously <pb facs="0049"
                                n="41" xml:id="pg41"/> adopted on September 27 by the Advisory
                            Committee of the League of Nations on the subject of aerial bombardment
                            by Japanese air forces of open towns in China.</p>
                        <p>The American Government, as has been set forth to the Japanese Government
                            repeatedly and especially in this Government’s note of September 22,
                            holds the view that any general bombing of an extensive area wherein
                            there resides a large populace engaged in peaceful pursuits is
                            unwarranted and contrary to principles of law and of humanity.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>If before there is an opportunity to have the statement quoted above presented to
                    the Assembly there should occur a meeting of the Advisory Committee you should
                    read the statement to the Advisory Committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
